      "assessment": "Treat the initial assessment as a hemorrhage emergency. Assess neurologic status, headache, vision, mucosal and menstrual bleeding, urine and stool blood, bruising, dyspnea, infection, and procedure sites while reviewing the smear and serial coagulation studies. After differentiation therapy starts, add frequent surveillance for fever, weight gain, edema, oxygen requirement, hypotension, kidney injury, and pulmonary findings.",
      "differential": "Differentiate APL from other acute myeloid leukemia subtypes, acute lymphoblastic leukemia, sepsis-associated DIC, thrombotic thrombocytopenic purpura and other microangiopathies, immune thrombocytopenia, liver-related coagulopathy, and medication-related bleeding. Rapid PML::RARA testing resolves the specific leukemia identity, but emergency retinoic-acid therapy should not wait when suspicion is high.",
