      "reviewStatus": "APPROVED",
      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-02",
      "definition": "Microscopic colitis is a chronic inflammatory disease of the colon that causes watery, usually nonbloody diarrhea even though the bowel lining may look normal during colonoscopy. Diagnosis requires mucosal biopsies because the defining inflammation is visible under the microscope rather than as the deep ulcers typical of Crohn disease or ulcerative colitis.",
