      "etiology": "The exact cause is usually not identifiable and likely reflects immune, genetic, microbiome, medication, and environmental interactions. Smoking and several medication groups are associated with microscopic colitis, including NSAIDs, proton-pump inhibitors, and selected serotonergic or other drugs; association does not prove that one medicine caused an individual case. Celiac disease, autoimmune thyroid disease, rheumatoid arthritis, psoriasis, and type 1 diabetes occur more often in affected patients.",
