      "assessment": "Assess stool onset, frequency, volume, nocturnal episodes, blood, urgency, incontinence, pain, fever, weight trend, intake, urine output, orthostatic symptoms, travel and infection exposure, autoimmune disease, smoking, and a complete medication timeline. Examine hydration and abdomen and assess perianal skin and fall risk. A normal visual colonoscopy does not close the assessment unless adequate regional biopsies were obtained.",
      "differential": "Differentiate microscopic colitis from infectious diarrhea including Clostridioides difficile, celiac disease, bile-acid diarrhea, irritable bowel syndrome with diarrhea, medication-induced diarrhea without colitis, Crohn disease, ulcerative colitis, hyperthyroidism, pancreatic insufficiency, small-intestinal bacterial overgrowth, and uncommon secretory disorders.",
