      "definition": "Diffuse large B-cell lymphoma is an aggressive mature B-cell non-Hodgkin lymphoma characterized by sheets of large abnormal lymphoid cells that grow diffusely and can enlarge quickly. The general ANI card focuses on DLBCL not otherwise specified; primary mediastinal, primary CNS, EBV-positive, transformed, and other defined entities require their own classification.",
      "pathology": "The tumor effaces normal lymph-node or extranodal architecture with large atypical B cells. Different molecular programs alter proliferation, B-cell-receptor and NF-kappa-B signaling, apoptosis, and immune escape, explaining why two tumors with the same broad name can behave differently and respond to different risk-adapted strategies.",
