      "prognosis": "Many children and fit younger adults can be cured with intensive risk-adapted treatment. Prognosis is less favorable with advanced age, very high tumor burden or LDH, CNS disease, organ dysfunction, inability to deliver planned therapy, or relapse. The speed of disease makes treatment urgency and supportive care inseparable.",
      "prevention": "There is no general screening test or vaccine. HIV prevention and treatment reduce one risk context, and malaria-control and EBV epidemiology matter in endemic regions, but they do not eliminate disease. Prevention within treatment focuses on tumor lysis, infection, infertility, and organ toxicity.",
