      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-02",
      "definition": "Babesiosis is infection of red blood cells by intraerythrocytic Babesia protozoa, most often Babesia microti in the United States. It ranges from asymptomatic infection to fever and hemolytic anemia or life-threatening shock, respiratory failure, renal injury, disseminated coagulation, and persistent relapsing disease in high-risk hosts.",
      "pathology": "Parasites enter erythrocytes and replicate, injuring or rupturing the cells. Direct hemolysis and immune clearance reduce circulating red-cell mass, while inflammatory and microvascular effects contribute to tissue hypoxia and organ dysfunction; lack of a functioning spleen permits much higher parasite burdens.",
