      "prevention": "Use EPA-registered repellent as appropriate, protective clothing, prompt bathing and tick checks, and safe tick removal. Blood-donor screening and deferral policies reduce transfusion transmission. There is no human vaccine, and a prior infection does not justify abandoning tick precautions.",
