      "etiology": "Most PCD is autosomal recessive, with less common X-linked or autosomal-dominant forms involving genes needed for motile-cilia structure or function. A known affected sibling is a strong diagnostic clue. Kartagener syndrome describes PCD with situs inversus and chronic sinopulmonary disease; it is not synonymous with every PCD phenotype.",
